TechFlow Codebase — Common Patterns Reference

Pattern: API Route Handler
```typescript
// app/api/documents/route.ts
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { getServerSession } from 'next-auth';
import { authOptions } from '@/lib/auth';

export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const session = await getServerSession(authOptions);
  if (!session) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
  }
  // ... fetch data
  return NextResponse.json({ data });
}
```

Pattern: Protected Server Component
```typescript
// app/(dashboard)/documents/page.tsx
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';
import { getServerSession } from 'next-auth';

export default async function DocumentsPage() {
  const session = await getServerSession();
  if (!session) redirect('/login');
  const documents = await fetchDocuments(session.user.id);
  return <DocumentList documents={documents} />;
}
```

Pattern: Client Component with Query
```typescript
'use client';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';

export function SearchResults({ query }: { query: string }) {
  const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ['search', query],
    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/search?q=${query}`).then(r => r.json()),
    enabled: query.length > 1,
  });
  if (isLoading) return <Skeleton />;
  if (error) return <Error message={error.message} />;
  return <ResultsList results={data.results} />;
}
```

Notes to self:
- ALWAYS check auth in API routes
- ALWAYS handle loading and error states
- ALWAYS add TypeScript types (no 'any')
- When in doubt, look at how Mike or Lisa wrote similar patterns
